---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adeptus Custodes Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Adeptus Custodes? Learn how the Emperor's golden warriors play, how to paint them, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🛡️</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Adeptus Custodes</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            The Emperor's personal bodyguard. Golden warriors of terrifying power, each one individually 
            crafted over centuries. The smallest army in 40k — and arguably the most elite.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Elite Melee</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160–$200</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-3 italic">Not recommended as a first army — but if you're drawn to them, read on.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Adeptus Custodes?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          The Adeptus Custodes are not Space Marines. This is the first thing to understand. 
          While Space Marines are produced in bulk — gene-seed implanted into recruits, 
          a hundred at a time — each Custodian is individually crafted by the Emperor himself 
          using processes so complex that no one else fully understands them.
        </p>
        <p>
          A Space Marine takes years to make. A Custodian takes centuries. Where a Chapter 
          fields a thousand warriors, the entire Custodes numbers around ten thousand — total, 
          across all of history. They are not a military force in any conventional sense. 
          They are a living weapon, each one the pinnacle of human potential.
        </p>
        <p>
          They wear Auramite armor — not ceramite like the Space Marines — a more resilient 
          alloy with a deep golden hue. They carry Guardian Spears: a long-handled powered 
          weapon with a bolter built into the haft. In close combat, a single Custodian can 
          tear through a squad of Space Marines without breaking stride.
        </p>
        <p>
          For ten thousand years, most of them never left Terra. Their duty was singular: 
          protect the Emperor, who sits dying-but-immortal on the Golden Throne, sustaining 
          the Astronomican that allows faster-than-light travel across the Imperium. 
          Since the return of Primarch Roboute Guilliman and the opening of the Great Rift, 
          more Custodians venture out into the galaxy — but they go where they judge it necessary, 
          answering to no one but the Emperor's own will.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          The Custodes play like nothing else in 40k. A typical army has <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">15–25 models total</strong>. 
          Not a squad of 15 — the whole army. Every single model is worth 60–100+ points. 
          You're not moving units; you're moving individuals.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each Custodian is extraordinarily tough. Their armor saves most hits, they have 
          a built-in Feel No Pain against mortal wounds, and they carry multiple wounds 
          each. Getting a Custodian off an objective takes real work. But lose two or three 
          in a bad turn and you may not recover.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their signature mechanic is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Martial Ka'tah</strong> — before each fight, 
          you select a combat stance. Dacatarai gives your weapons Sustained Hits 1 
          (great against hordes). Rendax gives Lethal Hits (great against monsters and vehicles). 
          Reading the game and choosing the right stance is a core decision you make constantly.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a high-skill-floor army. Every positioning decision matters. Every trade 
          matters. A beginner who loses a squad loses models worth 60 points. A Custodes 
          player who loses a bad engagement might lose 200 points in one turn. 
          But when you're winning — when your Allarus Custodians deep strike onto an objective 
          and tear through whatever was holding it — it feels like nothing else.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Custodes are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You want the most elite, powerful-feeling warriors in the setting</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy high-stakes, low-model-count play</li>
            <li>✓ You want an army where every model feels like a named hero</li>
            <li>✓ You love gold as an aesthetic — this army commits to it fully</li>
            <li>✓ You want something truly unique-looking on the table</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ This is your first army — the low model count is punishing to learn on</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde or lots of cheap models on the table</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer shooting-focused playstyles</li>
            <li>✗ You want a straightforward rules experience</li>
            <li>✗ Budget is a concern — Custodes models are expensive per model</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Adeptus Custodes</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Gold is the challenge. But there's a fast route and a slow route — both look great at table distance.
      </p>

      <!-- Fast route -->
      <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg mb-4 text-[#f0ede8]">The fast route (~20 min per model)</h3>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray with Retributor Armour</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Citadel's gold spray. Covers the whole model in one pass. This is your base coat — everything else builds on this.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash with Reikland Fleshade</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Apply over the whole model. Flows into the recesses of the armor and creates instant warmth and depth. The gold goes from flat to rich.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush with Liberator Gold</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A light drybrush over the raised armor panels brings out the edges and restores brightness. Don't overdo it — you want the shaded areas to stay dark.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint the cloak/plume red</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Khorne Red basecoat, Nuln Oil shade, Mephiston Red layer on raised areas. The red against gold is the classic Custodes look.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Silver for blades and weapons</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Leadbelcher on weapon blades and gun barrels. Nuln Oil wash. Stormhost Silver edge highlight on blade edges. Done.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Astrogranite Debris texture paint for a marble-esque palace floor look. Drybrush Administratum Grey. Add a tuft or two.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Contrast tip -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">Contrast paint shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Spray <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Wraithbone</strong>, then apply 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Iyanden Yellow Contrast</strong> mixed with 
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Nazdreg Yellow Contrast</strong> over the armor. 
          Then drybrush <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Stormhost Silver</strong> lightly for highlights. 
          Not the classic gold look but striking — a warm burnished metal. 
          Finish with red cloth and silver blades as above.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. At 14 models, it's already a significant portion of a full army.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Adeptus Custodes</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Includes a Blade Champion, 3 Allarus Custodians (the big terminators with halberds), 
          5 Custodian Guard, and 5 Custodian Wardens — 14 models total. 
          For an elite army, this is actually close to a full list. The Allarus can deep strike 
          behind enemy lines; the Guard hold objectives; the Wardens provide durable midfield presence.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D14W3KTM?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          See price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Trajann Valoris</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The Captain-General of the Custodes — their most powerful named character. 
          He's a force multiplier that makes nearby units hit harder and survive better. 
          A natural choice after the Combat Patrol, and a showpiece model to paint.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Trajann+Valoris+Warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Retributor Armour Spray', use: 'Base coat — the gold', required: true },
            { name: 'Reikland Fleshade', use: 'Shade wash — depth and warmth', required: true },
            { name: 'Liberator Gold', use: 'Drybrush — restore edge brightness', required: true },
            { name: 'Khorne Red', use: 'Cloaks and plumes', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher', use: 'Weapon blades and gun barrels', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade for red and silver areas', required: true },
            { name: 'Stormhost Silver', use: 'Edge highlights on blades', required: false },
            { name: 'Mephiston Red', use: 'Layer — restore red cloth highlights', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Adeptus Custodes', cost: '~$160', note: 'Blade Champion + Allarus + Guard + Wardens (14 models)' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$40', note: 'Gold spray + shades + layers + metallics' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey drybrush' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Custodes are larger models — plastic glue works too' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$237</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Good news: you need very few additional kits to reach a full army. 
        The Combat Patrol alone is close to playable at 1,000 points — a full game size.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">For the Emperor. Personally.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Fourteen models. Every one a demigod. If that's your speed, 
        grab the Combat Patrol and start with the five Custodian Guard before committing to the rest.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
